Reusable object authoring contracts (@ws-contract-object-authoring: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @workspace-contracts, #requires @ws-object-recipes, #requires @ws-behavior-authoring, #requires @ws-procedural-appearance, #requires @ws-cad-behavior, #requires @ws-object-controls, #requires @ws-authoring-experiments) { r_5WHAF91WTC9SARQB901AJZV150
Status: Pending. Owner approval, 2026-11-15: incorporate the Aveltuner-inspired general authoring proposal into Workspace. Users construct reusable objects whose form, appearance, actions and behavior are editable together while choosing supported simulation detail independently.

[Development graph](../Workspace-Development.lingua) owns scheduling. This Record joins six bounded provider exports and then contributes to full core acceptance. It introduces no new numerical solver, fantasy-specific object type or additional runtime.

## Rationale and scope

[Aveltuner's creator](https://www.reddit.com/r/magicbuilding/comments/1wq18y3/im_designing_a_magic_system_where_a_lot_of_magic/) describes an early project exploring editable formulas and a progression from using collected examples to understanding and modifying their workings. Treat that as design inspiration, not evidence of a shipped general editor. [Houdini's digital assets](https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/assets/intro.html) illustrate packaging a network and exposing selected parameters; no dependency or replacement frontend is selected here.

Adopt a connected native path: use a supplied object, adjust its public controls, inspect the recipe, change supported internals, expose useful controls, package and reuse it. The same families serve devices, mechanical assemblies, authoring tools, decorative effects and fictional objects. Source parameters, state and evaluation are real supported contracts; a descriptive label does not create a capability.

## Milestones and owners

- [ ] **OA.M01.** [Object recipes](../features/Object-Recipes.lingua) owns REC.T01–REC.T04: a reusable mesh recipe with typed public controls, editable internals, independent instances, source variants and accepted save/undo.
- [ ] **OA.M02.** [Behavior authoring](../features/Behavior-Authoring.lingua) owns BHV.T01–BHV.T05: native composition of supported events/state/timing/actions and bounded local trials with inspectable causes.
- [ ] **OA.M03.** [Procedural appearance](../features/Procedural-Appearance.lingua) owns VIS.T01–VIS.T04: reusable geometry/material/emission/curve and bounded trail/pulse controls proved with supplied inputs independently of a behavior runtime.
- [ ] **OA.M04.** [CAD bindings](../features/Cad-Behavior-Bindings.lingua) owns CBN.T01–CBN.T04: declared dimension/feature-to-behavior relationships and repair, without per-frame exact-CAD reconstruction.
- [ ] **OA.M05.** [Object controls](../features/Object-Control-Bindings.lingua) owns CTL.T01–CTL.T04: the same authored actions through native controls, connections, delegated operations and supported possession.
- [ ] **OA.M06.** [Authoring experiments](../features/Authoring-Experiments.lingua) owns AEX.T01–AEX.T04: real appearance/behavior binding, isolated comparison and causal explanation across the composed object.

## Shared contracts

- [ ] **OA.R01 — Existing families and bounded operators.** Reuse K1 definitions/occurrences, K4 quantities/fields, K6 operators, accepted commands, Rules/Signals/Areas, functional activities, appearance bindings and existing trace concepts. Re-audit actual implementation ownership before coding. Recipes contain supported versioned operators with known types, required capabilities, source provenance and measured resource limits. Import or composition does not execute arbitrary embedded code. No second save store, controller, universal language or permissions framework.
- [ ] **OA.R02 — Public interface and editable internals.** Distinguish parameters, actions, inputs, outputs and internal recipes. Expose a small usable interface while retaining stable source nodes, subrecipe boundaries and inspectable connections. Start from a preset, open/edit internals, group reusable fragments and promote selected controls through native forms and spatial tools. A diagram is an optional editing view over the same source, not a separate source of truth. Use ordinary selected-copy/shared-definition variants and pinned revisions.
- [ ] **OA.R03 — Typed meaning and source correspondence.** Validate quantity kinds, units, frames, reference roles, timing, ranges and capability requirements. A parameter sharing a label is not automatically the same quantity. Declare dependency directions and affected products. CAD/source features use existing stable selections and explicit ambiguous/deleted-reference repair; generated triangle order is not durable identity. Source edits invalidate affected results and derived evidence without replacing the last accepted source with failed or stale output.
- [ ] **OA.R04 — Separate execution semantics.** Construction dependencies are acyclic derivations; event/state behavior has explicit clocks, delay and bounded iteration; physical cycles use a supported domain solver; visual recipes use declared sampled inputs/cadence; control adapters route intents to the existing writer. Share interfaces and inspection, not an undifferentiated evaluator. Pure edit operations and async construction jobs retain K6 execution classes; live behavior uses existing activity scheduling. Runtime movement does not force CAD regeneration, and renderer frames do not become durable operational events.
- [ ] **OA.R05 — Action and activity lifecycle.** Specify activation/held update/release/cancel, timers/retrigger, temporary output lifetime, output ownership and stop conditions. Keep definition, occurrence settings and evolving state distinct. Editing a running definition uses a declared transfer or visible restart; source undo cannot rewind elapsed events. Bound queues, recursive expansion, children, particles, subscriptions and traces. One writer governs each output; cancellation, source generations, revoke and last demand retain their existing guarantees.
- [ ] **OA.R06 — Independent complexity and fidelity.** Editor disclosure, visual detail, structural residency, active behavior per domain, numerical accuracy and compute policy remain independently selectable. A single Activate control may drive a detailed implementation. Changing appearance or hiding internals cannot change physics. A cheap substitute must already implement required outputs, state mapping and applicable limits, or come from an independently supported reduction. Do not promise automatic equivalence of arbitrary recipes. Fictional imposed behavior, functional specification, measured evidence and simulated physical exchange retain distinct provenance.
- [ ] **OA.R07 — Input and possession parity.** Inspector buttons, native bindings, in-scene controls, functional connections and authorized Agent operations invoke the same typed actions. Possession supplies input to the selected model and preserves its authority/fidelity. Focus loss, release, target switch, revoke, stale revisions and disconnect terminate old held input. Place, temporary Play and explicitly supported live control remain distinct; Keep pose does not adopt a trial's event history or device side effects.
- [ ] **OA.R08 — Appearance and spatial authoring.** Support declared geometry/material/emission, temporal curves, regions/masks/falloffs and bounded transient visual outputs. Forms and in-scene handles edit the same origin/direction/region/curve source. Bind model observations to appearance explicitly with validity and clock semantics. A glow has no implicit heat/power; a visual cone is an observation of a detection region only when linked to that actual region. No physical material/force property is inferred from a visual label.
- [ ] **OA.R09 — CAD and operating behavior.** Shared dimensions may drive geometry, actuator limits and sensor regions through explicit maps. Separate formulas, persistent geometric constraints and physical equations. Invalid range/constraint/feature relationships remain repairable and cannot silently move unrelated parts or clamp live state. Preserve exact accepted construction dimensions while evaluating runtime pose and render products at their own cadence. Reusable construction tools publish accepted geometry only through ordinary preview/validation/undo.
- [ ] **OA.R10 — Experimentation and evidence.** Each provider includes its own native preview/cancel, save/reopen and meaningful diagnostics. Supported Run/Pause/Step/Reset, values/state/events and why-an-output-changed traces accompany behavior authoring; combined variant comparison joins later. Capture relevant source/input/clock/model/seed information, bound traces and distinguish unsupported diagnostics from false zero. Temporary trials cannot alter live source or emit external operational effects by default. Scientific Laboratory and long-term recording are not prerequisites for this authoring feedback.
- [ ] **OA.R11 — Native interaction and reuse.** Preserve ordinary selection/tree/inspector, precise numeric/spatial tools, accepted undo, shared/local overrides and explicit updates. Keep keyboard equivalents, readable status and reduced-motion options. Preserve the [edit-panel geometry requirement](../../../Lince.lingua): flush left, usable viewport height and reachable bottom-left controls. Required assets/operators/rights join the existing offline closure; unsupported definitions remain inspectable. A preview, successful compile or preset selection does not prove user-authored composition.
- [ ] **OA.R12 — Conservative scheduling and proof.** First prove the recipe interface with its actual mesh consumer, then branch appearance and behavior after their real providers. CAD bindings wait for CAD and behavior; custom possession actions wait for possession and behavior; composed experiments wait for appearance and behavior. No branch waits for unrelated globe/splat/character/scientific completion. Shared schemas, runtime/renderer/input code and performance windows have one owner; keep work in the current checkout. A discovered interface defect needs repair, but an already verified provider is not reopened merely to build a planned adapter.

## Canonical fixture and workflows

**OA.F01 — Three reusable creations.** Start with a signal-controlled lamp, a proximity-operated mesh hatch and an expanding visual pulse, with two occurrences of each relevant definition, known typed inputs and independently specified expected states/events. The lamp and hatch are ordinary nonfantasy cases. The pulse uses authored visual behavior and claims no force, heat or energy conservation. Include an invalid connection, a missing operator, a bounded temporary output and a reusable timer/envelope fragment. Freeze fixture rights, graph/object/operator/port counts, clocks, expansion/output limits, viewport and measured hardware budgets before implementation. CAD extends the hatch only after its own provider passes; possession extends actual supported actions later. No new numerical model is fixture setup.

| Workflow | Provider and milestone | Required evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| **OA.W01 — Use, open and reuse a recipe** | REC.T01–REC.T04; OA.M01 | Edit exposed mesh dimensions through forms and handles, open its internals, expose a control, group/reuse a fragment, fork one occurrence and save/undo/reopen. Invalid units/dependencies and stale outputs preserve accepted source; shared instances remain isolated. |
| **OA.W02 — Author how a device works** | BHV.T01–BHV.T05; OA.M02 | Compose lamp/hatch behavior, connect a trigger, replace a supported fragment, invoke exposed actions and trace expected state/timer changes. Preview/reset/cancel, offscreen demand, revision changes, loop limits and one writer are proved without physical solvers. |
| **OA.W03 — Author appearance independently** | VIS.T01–VIS.T04; OA.M03 | Edit pulse/indicator shapes, regions, curves and bounded transient visuals against supplied values/time. Save variants, lower visual detail, reject stale output and release products without changing source or inventing physical effects. |
| **OA.W04 — Bind construction to operation** | CBN.T01–CBN.T04; OA.M04 | Change the exact hatch width; validate construction and actuator/region mappings, repair a lost feature and handle incompatible live state. Check dimensions independently, undo/reopen and show that motion does not repeatedly run the CAD kernel. |
| **OA.W05 — Operate the same actions through different controls** | CTL.T01–CTL.T04; OA.M05 | Inspector, connection, delegated operation and possession reach the same public action. Remap controls, switch targets with held input and revoke. Preserve trial isolation, current model/authority and supported stop/release. |
| **OA.W06 — Understand and compare a composed creation** | AEX.T01–AEX.T04; OA.M06 | Connect real behavior outputs to appearance, compare isolated variants under captured input, inspect causes and cost, repair a binding and change render detail independently. Cancel/reopen and runtime recipe edits retain declared state/adoption semantics. |

## Acceptance and retained handoff

- [ ] **OA.P01.** Audit each package's real native/backend/persistence proof and operator limits. Use independent expected dimensions, event ordering and values rather than screenshots alone; inspect controls, diagnostic meaning and repair. Retain provider-specific unsupported cases and measured graph/output/queue/trace/cancellation budgets.
- [ ] **OA.P02.** Compose OA.W01–OA.W06 only when their actual providers exist. Run the lamp, hatch and pulse together with shared definitions and an identified editor/restricted observer; test stale/denied updates and offline reopen. Preserve selected models, source/privacy, one writer and scoped trials under aggregate admission. No new scientific worker is needed.
- [ ] **OA.P03.** Replay this bounded authoring capability in full core acceptance through 15.T09/15.W08, retaining every provider's verified subset and separate later domain adapters. Record source/build, native evidence, actual output accuracy, latency/resource observations, release and unresolved repairs. All milestones remain pending until observed; this plan edit implements no application capability.
